Keep the runner working on 32-bit ARM

Upstream phased out 32-bit ARM the hard way. The
actions_runner_deprecate_linux_arm32 and actions_runner_kill_linux_arm32
feature flags make the worker warn about and eventually refuse every
JavaScript action, and even without the flags a node24 action is
unconditionally downgraded to node20 because upstream never ships a
node24 binary for armv7l.

Short-circuit NodeUtil.CheckNodeVersionForLinuxArm32 so that 32-bit
ARM is treated like any other platform. This bypasses all of the
special-casing, so a node24 action just runs as usual, as long as there
is a node24 under externals/node24.

diff --git a/src/Runner.Common/Util/NodeUtil.cs b/src/Runner.Common/Util/NodeUtil.cs
index d87224f9..13750ef4 100644
--- a/src/Runner.Common/Util/NodeUtil.cs
+++ b/src/Runner.Common/Util/NodeUtil.cs
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@ namespace GitHub.Runner.Common.Util
             bool isArm32Linux = Constants.Runner.PlatformArchitecture.Equals(Constants.Architecture.Arm) &&
                                 Constants.Runner.Platform.Equals(Constants.OSPlatform.Linux);
 
-            if (!isArm32Linux)
+            if (true || !isArm32Linux)
             {
                 return (preferredVersion, null);
             }
